    "created_at": "2022-03-08T18:52:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-03-08T18:52:12Z",
    "body": "Chrome's current behavior is:\r\n1. A stylesheet is render-blocking only if it's inserted when the document doesn't have a body.\r\n2. Rendering starts when all the sheets (in step 1) are loaded and document has a body\r\n\r\nThe spec's behavior is:\r\nA. A stylesheet is render-blocking if it's inserted before the parser inserts a body\r\nB. Rendering starts when all the sheets (in step A) are loaded and parser has inserted a body\r\n\r\nSo if the page is like:\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<script>document.body = someElement;</script>\r\n<link rel=stylesheet href=\"...\">\r\n<link rel=stylesheet href=\"...\">\r\n<link rel=stylesheet href=\"...\">\r\n<body>\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe spec'ed behavior will delay the first paint by a lot.\r\n\r\nI haven't been able to run the exact test case locally, but I've confirmed that with [my WIP patch](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/3508823) and a [performance test result](https://pinpoint-dot-chromeperf.appspot.com/job/103fa8538a0000).",
